<BaseLayout title="How I evaluate evidence — Michael Rashkin" description="Evidence hierarchy, how I handle uncertainty, and how I separate population health from anecdotes.">
  <section class="container" style="padding-top: 38px;">
    <div class="prose">
      <h1>How I evaluate evidence</h1>

      <h2>My hierarchy in plain language</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Stronger evidence beats louder confidence.</strong></li>
        <li>RCTs, meta-analyses, guidelines, high-quality observational, mechanistic.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>What I watch for in nutrition research</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Measurement error</li>
        <li>Confounding</li>
        <li>Healthy user bias</li>
        <li>Adherence and dropout</li>
        <li>Real-world feasibility</li>
        <li>Absolute risk vs relative risk</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I separate population health from individual anecdotes</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>“A diet can ‘work’ for a person and fail at scale.”</li>
        <li>Focus on adherence, access, cost, environment.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I change my mind</h2>
      <p>
        Here’s what would change my position: better trials, better outcomes data, consistent replication, or a clear adverse signal.
      </p>

      <h2>How I handle uncertainty</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Use “Unclear” when appropriate.</li>
        <li>Explain why.</li>
      </ul>

      <hr />
      <p class="muted small">
        Note: this page is static in the starter. You can move it into Sanity later if you want full CMS control.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
